---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/sequenzy-vs-shopify-email';
const title = "Sequenzy vs Shopify Email: assess Shopify Messaging first";
const desc = "Compare an existing native workflow with a verified replacement, rather than assuming Shopify lacks automation.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does Shopify support abandoned checkout automation?",
    "answer": "Yes. Shopify documents automated checkout recovery and editing its workflow through Shopify Flow."
  },
  {
    "question": "Are native automation emails all free?",
    "answer": "No. Abandoned checkout emails are excluded from email charges; other marketing automation emails count toward the monthly allowance."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
<a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
<header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Sequenzy vs Shopify Email: assess Shopify Messaging first</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl">Compare an existing native workflow with a verified replacement, rather than assuming Shopify lacks automation.</p></header>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Shopify Email is now Shopify Messaging</h2>
<p>Shopify documents marketing automations in Messaging, including cart, checkout and browse recovery. The native option is therefore more than manual newsletters. Shopify Flow can support custom marketing workflows. Start by checking what is already active in your store; replacing a sender before inspecting native recovery can create duplicate messages.</p>
<h2>Distinguish cart from checkout recovery</h2>
<p>A cart without a started checkout and an abandoned checkout are different events. Shopify provides separate automations for them. For a proposed plant-shop evaluation, create one internal shopper in each state, then another who purchases before the delay ends. Record the workflow that entered and the message that was skipped. The native checkout documentation lists purchase and inventory conditions that can prevent delivery; a skipped email is not automatically a fault.</p>
<h2>Audit the native journey before rebuilding it</h2>
<p>In the admin, inventory each automation, its audience, delay, content and recent runs. Use Shopify Flow where the desired custom logic requires it. Write down a specific unresolved condition rather than a general desire for deeper lifecycle marketing. A proposed gift-order education branch, for example, requires an actual gift indicator. Verify the indicator exists and can be read at the right point in both systems before judging either builder.</p>
<h2>Where Sequenzy deserves evaluation</h2>
<p>Sequenzy advertises Shopify customer and order sync, automation and AI tooling. Evaluate it when those tools address an identified operating requirement. Try editing a real draft and explaining every entry and exit condition to the person who will maintain it. Confirm required order fields and account channel access. This review has not tested replenishment, gift logic or cross-flow suppression in either account and cannot promise a deployment time or recovery gain.</p>
<h2>Do not price free recovery as lost revenue</h2>
<p>Shopify currently includes a monthly email allowance on eligible plans, with usage charges beyond it; abandoned checkout emails are free and excluded from that allowance. Other marketing automation emails count toward it. Separate checkout recovery from ordinary campaigns when estimating your bill. Compare Sequenzy on the same campaign and automation workload, plus migration time and any channel add-ons. Attributed orders do not by themselves prove incremental profit.</p>
<h2>Replace one owner at a time</h2>
<p>Save native workflow settings and recent-run evidence before changes. Rebuild the selected journey with internal recipients, including purchase-during-delay and missing-field cases. Pause the corresponding native automation before enabling its replacement. Keep a rollback owner and a record of delayed messages in both systems. Stay with Shopify when the verified native journey meets the requirement; adopt Sequenzy when its demonstrated benefit warrants another service, irrespective of monthly order count.</p>
<h2>Sources and scope</h2>
<p>Checked November 25, 2026. Vendor documentation establishes advertised scope, not tested account behavior. Exercises above are proposed, not completed merchant tests.</p>
<ul>
<li><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/shopify-messaging/marketing-automations/create">Shopify marketing automations</a></li>
<li><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/migrate-abandoned-checkout">Shopify checkout recovery conditions</a></li>
<li><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/shopify-messaging/email/pricing">Shopify email billing rules</a></li>
<li><a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing">Sequenzy feature and channel scope</a></li>
<li><a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/sequenzy">Sequenzy Shopify listing</a></li>
</ul>
</article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-omnisend">Sequenzy vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-mailchimp">Sequenzy vs Mailchimp</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/print-on-demand">Email apps for print-on-demand</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Questions before choosing" />
</BaseLayout>
